# Normalize line endings across the whole repository.
#
# Without this file every tool that writes a file on Windows (editors, scripts,
# `cp`, agent tooling) can flip LF to CRLF, and git then reports the entire file
# as changed. That turned a 15-file change into a 105-file "diff" of 26k lines,
# making real history unreadable.
#
# `text=auto` lets git normalize to LF in the repository, and `eol=lf` forces LF
# in the working tree too, so the working tree and the index can never disagree
# about line endings again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalized or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webp binary

# Lockfiles are generated with LF and must stay byte-identical, otherwise every
# install produces a spurious diff.
package-lock.json -text
*.lock -text

# Batch/PowerShell on Windows expect CRLF to run correctly.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
